# Marquez walkthrough API verification

Generated 2026-09-11 against the live local port-forwards for the cluster
api.bgal-pool-ljt7l.aws.rh-ods.com.

The existing port-forward session was reused because port 5000 was already occupied.

## Setup

Command:

    MARQUEZ=http://127.0.0.1:5000
    REGISTRY=http://127.0.0.1:8081
    CLUSTER=api.bgal-pool-ljt7l.aws.rh-ods.com
    PROJECT=ol-best-practices
    REGISTRY_NS=dataregistry://$CLUSTER/$PROJECT
    ASSET_ID=$(curl --silent --fail "$REGISTRY/v1/assets" | jq -r '.[0].assetId')

Explanation: Points the queries at the local Marquez/registry forwards and discovers
the current registry asset ID.

Output:

    ASSET_ID=01a08bab-6620-75e4-97bd-b71dc2b99cf4

## 1. Namespace discovery

Command:

    curl --silent --fail "$MARQUEZ/api/v1/namespaces" \
      | jq '{namespaceCount: (.namespaces | length), namespaces: [.namespaces[]? | {name}]}'

Explanation: Confirms Marquez is reachable and lists materialized namespaces.

Output:

    {
      "namespaceCount": 6,
      "namespaces": [
        {"name": "dataregistry://api.bgal-pool-ljt7l.aws.rh-ods.com/ol-best-practices"},
        {"name": "dch-mock://api.bgal-pool-ljt7l.aws.rh-ods.com/ol-best-practices"},
        {"name": "default"},
        {"name": "kfp://api.bgal-pool-ljt7l.aws.rh-ods.com/ol-best-practices"},
        {"name": "s3://sample-data"},
        {"name": "spark://api.bgal-pool-ljt7l.aws.rh-ods.com/ol-best-practices"}
      ]
    }

## 2. RunEvent download

Command:

    curl --silent --fail \
      "$MARQUEZ/api/v1/events/lineage?limit=10000&sort=asc" \
      > /tmp/marquez-lineage.json

Explanation: Downloads the RunEvent history used by the subsequent jq queries.
The raw response was retained at /tmp/marquez-lineage.json during verification.

Summary command:

    jq '{totalCount, returned: (.events | length),
      first: (.events[0] | {eventType,eventTime,runId:.run.runId,
      job: (.job.namespace + " / " + .job.name)}),
      last: (.events[-1] | {eventType,eventTime,runId:.run.runId,
      job: (.job.namespace + " / " + .job.name)})}' /tmp/marquez-lineage.json

Output:

    {
      "totalCount": 485,
      "returned": 483,
      "first": {
        "eventType": "FAIL",
        "eventTime": "2026-09-10T16:32:59.182815Z",
        "runId": "2ab6d826-7425-43f2-a27d-6956b03bab55",
        "job": "kfp://api.bgal-pool-ljt7l.aws.rh-ods.com/ol-best-practices / sample-app-best-practices"
      },
      "last": {
        "eventType": "START",
        "eventTime": "2026-09-10T14:14:49.708639Z",
        "runId": "769dd4fe-40b8-583d-9ec2-ee4cd8442328",
        "job": "kfp://api.bgal-pool-ljt7l.aws.rh-ods.com/ol-best-practices / sample-app-best-practices"
      }
    }

Command:

    jq -r '.events[] |
      [.eventTime, .eventType, .run.runId, .job.namespace, .job.name] |
      @tsv' /tmp/marquez-lineage.json | sed -n '1,8p'

Explanation: Shows a compact sample of event state, run ID, and job identity.

Output:

    2026-09-10T16:32:59.182815Z  FAIL      2ab6d826-7425-43f2-a27d-6956b03bab55  kfp://.../ol-best-practices  sample-app-best-practices
    2026-09-10T16:32:38.343315Z  FAIL      01a08c2a-0181-752b-a87c-3eb8a7b47ae2  kfp://.../ol-best-practices  create-mock-embeddings
    2026-09-10T16:32:38.273945Z  START     01a08c2a-0181-752b-a87c-3eb8a7b47ae2  kfp://.../ol-best-practices  create-mock-embeddings
    2026-09-10T16:32:18.542728Z  FAIL      01a08c29-b425-7e09-a54e-4b49d55a4f54  kfp://.../ol-best-practices  create-mock-embeddings
    2026-09-10T16:32:18.469658Z  START     01a08c29-b425-7e09-a54e-4b49d55a4f54  kfp://.../ol-best-practices  create-mock-embeddings
    2026-09-10T16:31:47.471Z       COMPLETE  01a08c28-bff8-78bd-a01f-cafd3e095f06  spark://.../ol-best-practices  transform_documents
    2026-09-10T16:31:47.468Z       COMPLETE  01a08c29-31a5-7899-8ee1-a0bb7232aa80  spark://.../ol-best-practices  transform_documents.execute_insert_into_hadoop_fs_relation_command
    2026-09-10T16:31:47.24Z        RUNNING   01a08c29-31a5-7899-8ee1-a0bb7232aa80  spark://.../ol-best-practices  transform_documents.execute_insert_into_hadoop_fs_relation_command

Verification note: the API returned newest-first even though sort=asc was supplied.
The guide must not assume that the returned array is chronological.

## 3. Registry metadata

Command:

    curl --silent --fail "$REGISTRY/v1/assets" \
      | jq 'map({assetId,name,owner,location,lineageStatus})'

Explanation: Reads customer-facing registry metadata for joining to lineage.

Output:

    [
      {
        "assetId": "01a08bab-6620-75e4-97bd-b71dc2b99cf4",
        "name": "Customer documents",
        "owner": "data-science",
        "location": "s3://sample-data/raw/documents.csv",
        "lineageStatus": "DELIVERED"
      }
    ]

## 4. Materialized registry dataset and symlink

Commands:

    NS_ENCODED=$(jq -rn --arg v "$REGISTRY_NS" '$v|@uri')
    NAME_ENCODED=$(jq -rn --arg v "$ASSET_ID" '$v|@uri')

    curl --silent --fail \
      "$MARQUEZ/api/v1/namespaces/$NS_ENCODED/datasets/$NAME_ENCODED" \
      | jq '{namespace,name,facets: {documentation: .facets.documentation,
      ownership: .facets.ownership,
      lifecycleStateChange: .facets.lifecycleStateChange,
      symlinks: .facets.symlinks, datasetType: .facets.datasetType}}'

Explanation: Reads the logical registry dataset and the useful DatasetEvent facets.

Output:

    {
      "namespace": "dataregistry://api.bgal-pool-ljt7l.aws.rh-ods.com/ol-best-practices",
      "name": "01a08bab-6620-75e4-97bd-b71dc2b99cf4",
      "facets": {
        "documentation": {
          "description": "Mutable CSV source with no durable row or content identifier"
        },
        "ownership": {"owners": [{"name": "data-science", "type": "MAINTAINER"}]},
        "lifecycleStateChange": {"lifecycleStateChange": "CREATE"},
        "symlinks": {
          "identifiers": [
            {"name": "raw/documents.csv", "type": "OBJECT", "namespace": "s3://sample-data"}
          ]
        },
        "datasetType": {"datasetType": "FILE"}
      }
    }

Command:

    curl --silent --fail \
      "$MARQUEZ/api/v1/namespaces/$NS_ENCODED/datasets/$NAME_ENCODED" \
      | jq '.facets.symlinks.identifiers'

Explanation: Extracts the logical-to-physical alias.

Output:

    [
      {
        "name": "raw/documents.csv",
        "type": "OBJECT",
        "namespace": "s3://sample-data"
      }
    ]

## 5. Event state and correlation

Command:

    jq '[.events[].eventType] | group_by(.) |
      map({eventType: .[0], count: length})' /tmp/marquez-lineage.json

Explanation: Counts lifecycle event states in the retained RunEvent history.

Output:

    [
      {"eventType": "COMPLETE", "count": 168},
      {"eventType": "FAIL", "count": 31},
      {"eventType": "RUNNING", "count": 106},
      {"eventType": "START", "count": 178}
    ]

Command:

    jq '{failedOrAborted: [.events[] |
      select(.eventType == "FAIL" or .eventType == "ABORT")] | length}' \
      /tmp/marquez-lineage.json

Explanation: Counts failed or aborted attempts.

Output:

    {"failedOrAborted": 31}

Command:

    jq '{withParent: [.events[] |
      select(.run.facets.parent != null)] | length}' /tmp/marquez-lineage.json

Explanation: Counts events with a parent execution relationship.

Output:

    {"withParent": 433}

## 6. Raw-source consumers

Command:

    RAW_NS=s3://sample-data
    RAW_NAME=raw/documents.csv

    jq --arg ns "$RAW_NS" --arg name "$RAW_NAME" '
      .events[]
      | select(any(.inputs[]?; .namespace == $ns and .name == $name))
      | {eventTime,eventType,
         job: (.job.namespace + " / " + .job.name),
         runId: .run.runId,
         outputs: [.outputs[]? | .namespace + " / " + .name]}' \
      /tmp/marquez-lineage.json

Explanation: Finds RunEvents that report consuming the raw S3 dataset.

Output sample:

    {
      "eventTime": "2026-09-10T16:30:56.362481Z",
      "eventType": "COMPLETE",
      "job": "dch-mock://api.bgal-pool-ljt7l.aws.rh-ods.com/ol-best-practices / read-and-stage",
      "runId": "01a08c28-7222-757c-be3f-9f84226ef4cf",
      "outputs": [
        "s3://sample-data / staging/01a08bab-6620-75e4-97bd-b71dc2b99cf4/documents.csv"
      ]
    }

The same query also returned the START event for this run and additional historical
read-and-stage runs. The complete output was intentionally not duplicated here.

## 7. Parameters and output metadata

Command:

    jq '.events[]
      | select(.run.facets.executionParameters != null)
      | {runId: .run.runId,
         job: (.job.namespace + " / " + .job.name),
         parameters: .run.facets.executionParameters.parameters}' \
      /tmp/marquez-lineage.json

Explanation: Reads embedded asset, algorithm, dimensions, and mock/real parameters.

Output sample:

    {
      "runId": "01a08c2a-0181-752b-a87c-3eb8a7b47ae2",
      "job": "kfp://api.bgal-pool-ljt7l.aws.rh-ods.com/ol-best-practices / create-mock-embeddings",
      "parameters": [
        {"key": "algorithm", "value": "sha256-demo"},
        {"key": "assetId", "value": "01a08bab-6620-75e4-97bd-b71dc2b99cf4"},
        {"key": "dimensions", "value": "8"},
        {"key": "mock", "value": "true"}
      ]
    }

Command:

    jq '.events[] | .outputs[]?
      | select(.facets.schema != null or .facets.columnLineage != null)
      | {dataset: (.namespace + " / " + .name),
         schema: .facets.schema,
         statistics: .outputFacets.outputStatistics}' \
      /tmp/marquez-lineage.json

Explanation: Reads declared output schema and statistics.

Output sample:

    {
      "dataset": "s3://sample-data / transformed/01a08bab-6620-75e4-97bd-b71dc2b99cf4/01a08c28-bff8-78bd-a01f-cafd3e095f06",
      "schema": {
        "fields": [
          {"name": "title", "type": "string"},
          {"name": "category", "type": "string"},
          {"name": "normalized_text", "type": "string"},
          {"name": "word_count", "type": "integer"}
        ]
      },
      "statistics": {"size": 1975, "rowCount": 4, "fileCount": 1}
    }

## 8. Registry lookup correction

Command from the document:

    curl --silent --fail "$REGISTRY/$ASSET_ID" \
      | jq '{assetId,name,owner,description,location,lineageStatus}'

Explanation: This was intended to read the registry record by ID, but the path is
missing /v1/assets/.

Output:

    curl: (22) The requested URL returned error: 404

Corrected command:

    curl --silent --fail "$REGISTRY/v1/assets/$ASSET_ID" \
      | jq '{assetId,name,owner,description,location,lineageStatus}'

Explanation: Uses the actual registry API route.

Output:

    {
      "assetId": "01a08bab-6620-75e4-97bd-b71dc2b99cf4",
      "name": "Customer documents",
      "owner": "data-science",
      "description": "Mutable CSV source with no durable row or content identifier",
      "location": "s3://sample-data/raw/documents.csv",
      "lineageStatus": "DELIVERED"
    }

## 9. Distinct job identities

Command:

    jq -r '.events[] | [.job.namespace, .job.name] | @tsv' \
      /tmp/marquez-lineage.json | sort -u

Explanation: Lists stable component identities represented in Marquez.

Output:

    dch-mock://api.bgal-pool-ljt7l.aws.rh-ods.com/ol-best-practices  read-and-stage
    kfp://api.bgal-pool-ljt7l.aws.rh-ods.com/ol-best-practices  create-mock-embeddings
    kfp://api.bgal-pool-ljt7l.aws.rh-ods.com/ol-best-practices  sample-app-best-practices
    spark://api.bgal-pool-ljt7l.aws.rh-ods.com/ol-best-practices transform_documents
    spark://api.bgal-pool-ljt7l.aws.rh-ods.com/ol-best-practices transform_documents.collect_limit
    spark://api.bgal-pool-ljt7l.aws.rh-ods.com/ol-best-practices transform_documents.deserialize_to_object
    spark://api.bgal-pool-ljt7l.aws.rh-ods.com/ol-best-practices transform_documents.execute_insert_into_hadoop_fs_relation_command

## Verification summary

Verified:

- Marquez API is reachable.
- Six namespaces are materialized.
- The API reports 485 total RunEvents and returned 483 for the query.
- The registry asset is delivered.
- UUID 01a08bab-6620-75e4-97bd-b71dc2b99cf4 resolves to Customer documents.
- Registry ownership is data-science.
- The symlink points to s3://sample-data/raw/documents.csv.
- COMPLETE, FAIL, RUNNING, and START events are present.
- Parent correlation is present.
- The raw source is consumed by read-and-stage.
- Spark schema/statistics and embedding parameters are present.

Corrections required in the walkthrough:

1. Registry lookup must use /v1/assets/<asset-id>.
2. Do not describe the returned events array as chronological when using sort=asc;
   this live Marquez response was newest-first.
3. Marquez contains technical Spark jobs in addition to the logical application stages.

## 10. Historical UUID from the original Marquez URL

Command from the walkthrough's original example:

    OLD_ASSET_ID=01a08ba1-af04-7394-b90a-cc1557dc8b30
    curl --silent --show-error --fail \
      "$MARQUEZ/api/v1/namespaces/$NS_ENCODED/datasets/$OLD_NAME_ENCODED" \
      | jq '{namespace,name,facets}'

Output: Marquez still returns the dataset entity and its symlink to
s3://sample-data/raw/documents.csv.

Command:

    curl --silent --show-error --fail \
      "$REGISTRY/v1/assets/$OLD_ASSET_ID" \
      | jq '{assetId,name,owner,location,lineageStatus}'

Output:

    curl: (22) The requested URL returned error: 404

The current registry asset discovered from GET /v1/assets is
01a08bab-6620-75e4-97bd-b71dc2b99cf4. Therefore the original UUID is historical
Marquez lineage, not the current registry record. The walkthrough now discovers
the current asset dynamically.
